# Verilog define for PLL instantiation
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "QUARTUS=1"
# DVD-FORK DEBUG: to bring back the Atmosfear wrong-title diagnosis overlay
# (dvd/debug_overlay.sv rows 21..26; O[2] + Disc Menus On to view), uncomment the
# next line and rebuild (--compile). It re-tightens the congested fit and may
# need a fitter seed re-sweep. Left OFF for the release build.
# set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "DEBUG_OVERLAY=1"
# NOTE (Film 24p, issue #124): DEBUG_OVERLAY was briefly re-enabled here for the
# bring-up lates readout, but the overlay+Phase1 netlist fit flaky on SEED 9 (routed +
# STA-clean but HW-green — the framebuffer write path came out functionally broken).
# Ship the release (no-overlay) netlist, which has headroom and fits SEED 9 cleanly.
# Re-add `VERILOG_MACRO "DEBUG_OVERLAY=1"` + seed-sweep if the numeric overlay is needed.

set_instance_assignment -name PARTITION_HIERARCHY root_partition -to | -section_id Top
set_global_assignment -name FITTER_AGGRESSIVE_ROUTABILITY_OPTIMIZATION ALWAYS
# DVD-FORK (frame-drop reland): this design is congestion-marginal (a routing lottery).
# On this exact netlist (frame-drop + all congestion cuts + physical synthesis OFF), the
# DEFAULT seed and seeds 2/3/4 all FAILED to route; SEED 5 routes. Pinned so a full
# `build_release.sh --compile` reproduces the routable result. NOTE: this seed is tied to
# THIS netlist — any RTL change may need a re-sweep (see tools/seed_sweep.sh). The real fix
# is structural (LogicLock / targeted fringe fix) — see docs/roadmap.md cleanup section.
set_global_assignment -name ROUTER_TIMING_OPTIMIZATION_LEVEL NORMAL
# Physical synthesis: lifts the decode-domain (clk_dec, 81 MHz) Fmax from ~80 -> ~92 MHz by
# rebalancing the limiting path (high-fanout mem_req_wr_almost_full -> framestore_request
# priority mux -> STATE_RECON). Without this, 81 MHz over-clocks the domain (raw Fmax ~80)
# -> intermittent green chroma fringe. HW-CONFIRMED 2026-07-01: 81 runs fringe-free at full
# compute, +~137 ALMs -- BUT it inflates routing design-wide and, on top of the frame-drop
# reland, tips the (congestion-marginal) design over the routing edge (Error 11802 at 78%
# ALMs; 5 builds failed even after removing decoder_profile + UART + baking O[14/15/18]).
# *** TEMPORARILY OFF (2026-07-01, feature/frame-drop-reland) *** to route THIS diagnostic
# build for the frame-drop rows-14/15 HW read. Tradeoff (user-approved): the green chroma
# fringe returns, but it is cosmetic and does NOT affect the frame-drop pacing test or the
# counter read. The proper fix is the TARGETED fringe fix (MAX_FANOUT / duplicated register
# on the mem_req_wr_almost_full net) instead of this global switch -- see docs/roadmap.md
# "FPGA congestion / resource cleanup". Flip these back ON (or do the targeted fix) for a
# clean release build.
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_REGISTER_RETIMING OFF
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_REGISTER_DUPLICATION OFF
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_COMBO_LOGIC OFF

# DVD-FORK (frame-drop reland): the design is routing-marginal (a congestion lottery). To
# route the frame-drop feature we removed decoder_profile + the debug UART, baked the settled
# O[14/15/18] toggles to constants, turned physical synthesis OFF (see above), and pin a
# fitter SEED. The seed is tied to the EXACT netlist and it's a genuine lottery: pre-debt-decay
# needed SEED 5; the debt-decay netlist took SEED 2; the (removed) decay-knob netlist had seeds
# 2/3/6 GRIND while SEED 7 routed; the FINAL no-decay/no-knob netlist (decay reverted) also
# routed on SEED 7 (~12 min). Any RTL change may need a re-sweep (tools/seed_sweep.sh, per-fit
# timeout). The real fix is structural
# (LogicLock / targeted fringe fix) — see docs/roadmap.md cleanup section + memory
# quartus-build-flaky-routing.
#
# SUBPICTURE netlist (PR #71, 2026-07-06): SEED 7 FROZE playback / caused constant resync on
# HW (the renderer landed in the display hotspot). SEED 9 is the HW-CONFIRMED value for this
# netlist (build DVD_subpic_rel: combinational blend + debug_overlay compiled OUT via
# `ifdef DEBUG_OVERLAY). Defining DEBUG_OVERLAY re-tightens the fit and likely needs a new sweep.
#
# TIMED-STILLS netlist (2026-07-09): SEED 7 re-pinned after SEED 9 striped on HW. The
# "clk_dec Fmax 110.24 MHz" claimed in that pin commit is JUNK — the sweep's extraction read a
# neighboring clock's row (Fmax tables sort by value; see tools/fmax_check.sh header). The
# MEASURED truth for SEED 7 on this netlist: clk_dec 81.41 MHz @100C / 78.0 @-40C = MARGINAL
# (fringe lottery). Verify every fit with tools/fmax_check.sh; build_release.sh --release
# gates on it. Seed choice is only trustworthy when that check passes at both slow corners.
# SCRUB-VOBU-ALIGN netlist (PR #106, 2026-07-10): the new NAV-align probe states perturbed the
# netlist enough that SEED 7 could no longer place legally (100% LABs used; "Can't fit design in
# device"). Re-swept: SEED 9 routed but MARGINAL (76.8 MHz @100C = fail), SEED 13 routes with
# good margin (clk_dec 94.36 MHz @100C / 90.19 MHz @-40C = PASS). Pinned SEED 13.
# AC3-AREA + DTS netlist (feature/ac3-area-reduction, 2026-07-11): the M19 area pass
# (35,844 ALMs = 86%, DSP 91) + re-enabled DTS chain changed the netlist again — SEED 13
# failed to route; re-swept and SEED 7 routes with margin (clk_dec 86.07 MHz @100C /
# 88.32 MHz @-40C = PASS both corners). Pinned SEED 7.
# FORCE-4:3-SUBPICS netlist (PR #115, 2026-07-12): the P1O[15] subpicture display-mode
# override added a shared-mux path in emu.sv; SEED 9 (the white-rabbit pin) then failed to
# route ("Can't fit", 99% LABs). Re-swept: SEED 7 TIMED OUT (grind), SEED 11 routes with good
# margin (clk_dec 91.58 MHz @100C / 89.52 MHz @-40C = PASS both corners). Pinned SEED 11.
# FORCE-4:3 WINDOWLESS-FLIPBOOK fix (PR #115 round 2, 2026-07-12): driving spu_decode.menu_mode
# from force_43_subp (so the MiB commentary 15fps flipbook shows windowless) perturbed the
# netlist again -> SEED 11/13/5 failed to route; SEED 8 routes with margin (clk_dec 92.25 MHz
# @100C / 88.62 MHz @-40C = PASS both corners). Pinned SEED 8.
# MENU-CLEAN netlist (PR #116, 2026-07-12): removed the flush primer + restored the cold
# re-decode (menu_snap fast trigger) + §5c deep-menu-flush toggle + menu-audio free-run. This
# reshuffled placement -> SEED 8 failed to route ("Can't fit", 86% ALM = congestion, not
# capacity). Re-swept (USE_DOCKER seed_sweep): SEED 7 TIMED OUT, SEED 9 routes + PASSES both
# corners (clk_dec 84.42 MHz @100C / 88.43 MHz @-40C). Pinned SEED 9. NOTE: 84.42 is a real
# pass (>81 both corners) but a tighter margin than recent builds; if HW shows striping/green,
# re-sweep for a higher-margin seed (SWEEP_ALL=1).
# MENU-UNIVERSAL netlist (2026-07-13, §5d): audio-continuity (aud_flush gated by keep_vbuf)
# + menu VBUF cap (reader throttle) added logic; congestion rose to the routing EDGE - the full
# `--compile` fit FAILED to route on SEED 9, but a bare `quartus_fit --seed=9` (the sweep) DID
# route and passed Fmax with margin (clk_dec 93.05 MHz @100C / 88.61 MHz @-40C). Pinned SEED 9.
# ⚠️ MARGINAL: `build_release --compile` may fail to route (use tools/seed_sweep.sh instead), and
# if HW shows green/garble, re-sweep SWEEP_ALL=1 for a more robust seed (or relieve congestion,
# e.g. remove the P1O[18] toggle once Smooth is confirmed universal).
# MENU-UNIVERSAL v2 netlist (2026-07-13): removed the P1O[18] toggle + moved the AC-3/DTS
# reframers off pipe_rst_n onto reset_n (pop fix). That relieved the congestion the v1 build hit
# (all seeds failed to route), and `--compile` now routes on SEED 9 DIRECTLY (no sweep) with a
# healthy margin (clk_dec 86.32 MHz @100C / 86.82 MHz @-40C). SEED 9 confirmed for this netlist.
# FILM 24p AUTO netlist (2026-07-25, feature/film-24p-auto): added the film cadence detector
# (resample_addrgen) + PAL-25p modeline/STC + the P1O[25:24] Off/On/Auto resolve — reshuffled
# placement so the QSF-pinned SEED 13 (v1) FAILED to route on `--compile` (86% ALM = congestion,
# not capacity). Re-swept (USE_DOCKER tools/seed_sweep.sh): SEED 9 routes + PASSES both corners
# (clk_dec 85.93 MHz @100C / 83.06 MHz @-40C). Pinned SEED 9. Same lottery caveat as above.
# TAIL-DRAIN netlist (2026-07-30, feature/pgc-end-tail-drain PR #149): the drain-wait gate +
# DRAIN_WD counter reshuffled placement -> the dual-raster pin SEED 5 FAILED to route on
# `--compile` (88% ALM = congestion, not capacity). Re-swept (USE_DOCKER tools/seed_sweep.sh):
# SEED 7 no-route; SEED 9 routes + PASSES both corners (clk_dec 86.62 MHz @100C / 87.69 MHz
# @-40C). Pinned SEED 9. Same lottery caveat as above.
#
# TAIL-DRAIN PHASE B netlist (2026-07-30, PR #150): the provenance gating (jnat/snat +
# nat_wait plumbing) reshuffled placement — the pinned SEED 9 routed but came in MARGINAL
# (clk_dec 80.22 MHz @100C < the 81.0 gate). Re-swept at FIT_TIMEOUT=3600 (healthy fits
# now take ~28-32 min; the old 2100 s cut killed viable seeds mid-fit): SEED 7 79.03
# marginal; SEED 5 no-route; SEED 11/13 previously timed out; SEED 8 routes + PASSES both
# corners (clk_dec 85.79 MHz @100C / 90.17 MHz @-40C). Pinned SEED 8. Same lottery caveat.
#
# PHASE B ROUND 2 netlist (2026-07-31, the nat_src TR-skip fix): SEED 8 went MARGINAL
# (clk_dec 80.37 MHz @100C). Re-swept: SEED 7 routes + PASSES both corners (clk_dec
# 85.38 MHz @100C / 90.26 MHz @-40C). Pinned SEED 7. Same lottery caveat.
#   ^ NOTE: that entry says "Pinned SEED 7" but the assignment on main read SEED 9 — one of
#   the two was stale. Recorded here rather than silently corrected, since it means the
#   as-built seed for the Phase-B netlist is ambiguous in this ledger.
#
# CROP 2-TAP netlist (2026-08-01, disp_hstretch output-driven resample + crt_ov_map rounding
# inverse, docs/crt_anamorphic.md SS8b): the pinned SEED 9 FAILED TO ROUTE on `--compile`, and
# so did SEED 7 in the sweep. NOT capacity — ALMs NEEDED went 37,196 -> 37,261 (+65, still
# 89%) and the SEED 11 fit actually lands LOWER at 37,147; placement succeeded and the ROUTER
# gave up on congestion (Warning 16618 / Critical Warning 188026, which names "changing the
# fitter seed" as the remedy; FITTER_AGGRESSIVE_ROUTABILITY_OPTIMIZATION is already ALWAYS).
# DSP 91 -> 94 (the three 9x8 blend multiplies). Re-swept (USE_DOCKER, FIT_TIMEOUT=3600):
# SEED 11 routes + PASSES both corners (clk_dec 82.82 MHz @100C / 87.34 MHz @-40C).
# Pinned SEED 11. Same lottery caveat as above.
#   ^ 82.82 is the LOWEST passing worst-corner value in this ledger (the others sit 84.4-94),
#   so a MARGIN SWEEP was run over every remaining seed (SWEEP_ALL=1, FMAX_MIN=83.5). Result:
#   SEED 13 no-route; SEED 5 77.57; SEED 8 74.47; SEED 17 81.73 @100C. So SEED 11's 82.82 is
#   the BEST of all seven seeds tried (9/7/13 no-route, 5/8/17 lower) — this netlist simply
#   sits lower than its predecessors, and 82.82 is the TOP of the distribution, not a lucky
#   marginal first hit. ✅ HW-CONFIRMED clean on 2026-08-01 (no fringing, Crop correct), so
#   SEED 11 is the as-built value — do NOT re-pin without a fresh HW test, since a different
#   seed is a different placement and would discard that confirmation.
#
# SDC CLOCK-GROUPS netlist (2026-08-01, feature/fringe-sdc-clock-groups): sys_top.sdc's
# set_clock_groups finally matches this fork's PLL (emu|sys_pll had matched NO group, so
# ~40k unclosable async crossings were fully timed — see docs/history.md §10). Same RTL
# as the Crop 2-tap netlist above; only the SDC changed. The fitter stopped chasing
# impossible CDC TNS: fits dropped ~30 min -> ~12 min AND the lottery collapsed —
# full sweep (SWEEP_ALL=1, FMAX_MIN=83.5, seeds 7 9 13 5 8 17 23 1 29 42): ALL TEN
# routed AND passed, worst-corner 86.87 (17) .. 92.46 (29); on the pre-fix netlist
# 7/9/13 were no-routes and the best was 82.82. Pinned SEED 29 (95.35 @100C /
# 92.46 @-40C = +14% margin over 81). Release gate raised to FMAX_MIN 86.0 (below the
# whole healthy distribution, well above the 81-83 marginal class that fringes).
# ✅ HW-CONFIRMED 2026-08-01 (PR #156): fringe gone, playback clean, S/PDIF OK — SEED 29
# is the as-built value; do NOT re-pin without a fresh HW test.
#
# FILM-24p EXACT-RATE netlist (2026-08-02, PR #158): the modeline constant change
# (875x1287) reshuffled placement enough that SEED 29 came in just under the gate —
# clk_dec 90.16 MHz @100C / 85.98 @-40C vs FMAX_MIN 86.0 (a 0.02 MHz miss at the cold
# corner, i.e. the ordinary post-SDC-fix spread, not a degraded netlist). Re-swept
# (USE_DOCKER tools/seed_sweep.sh): SEED 7 routes and PASSES both corners
# (clk_dec 92.02 MHz @100C / 88.39 MHz @-40C). Pinned SEED 7.
#   ^ NOTE: that entry says "Pinned SEED 7" but the assignment below read SEED 9 when the
#   sd-2048 branch forked — the same log/assignment mismatch pattern as the 2026-07-31 note.
#
# SD-2048-BLOCK netlist (2026-08-04, feature/sd-2048-blocks, BLKSZ=4 reader rework): the
# `--compile` fit came in MARGINAL (clk_dec 88.66 MHz @100C / 84.66 @-40C — cold corner
# under the 86.0 gate). Re-swept (USE_DOCKER tools/seed_sweep.sh, FMAX_MIN=86.0): SEED 7
# 88.66/84.66 marginal; SEED 9 routes + PASSES both corners (clk_dec 91.49 MHz @100C /
# 86.85 MHz @-40C). Pinned SEED 9 (assignment unchanged). Same lottery caveat as above.
#   ^ NOTE: despite that "Pinned SEED 9", the assignment below was COMMITTED as SEED 7 —
#   the comment/assignment mismatch pattern AGAIN (third occurrence). Root cause of the
#   pattern: `quartus_fit --seed=N` WRITES the SEED assignment back into this qsf, so a
#   sweep updates the file silently and whether the pin lands in git depends on whether
#   that session committed the qsf. Rule: after any sweep, `git diff DVD.qsf` and commit
#   the winning seed WITH the branch.
#
# CSS-DETECT netlist (2026-08-06, feature/css-detect-warn, PR #160): `--compile` with the
# committed SEED 7 came in MARGINAL (clk_dec 87.05 MHz @100C / 84.59 @-40C). Re-swept
# (FMAX_MIN=86.0): SEED 7 marginal (same numbers), SEED 9 PASSES both corners
# (clk_dec 89.06 MHz @100C / 88.07 MHz @-40C). Pinned SEED 9 (this time in git).
#
# FAILURE-MESSAGING netlist (2026-08-23, feature/failure-messaging, PR #180): the Phase-2
# popups add ~+93 ALMs to an already 90%-full fit. `--compile` on the inherited SEED 9 came
# in MARGINAL (clk_dec 89.59 MHz @100C / 85.79 @-40C — cold corner 0.2 MHz under the gate,
# and build_release.sh tagged the rbf MARGINAL). Re-swept (FMAX_MIN=86.0): SEED 7 PASSES
# both corners on THIS netlist (clk_dec 91.73 MHz @100C / 88.21 MHz @-40C) and was the
# first seed tried. Pinned SEED 7, committed with the branch per the rule above.
#   ^ NOTE the reversal vs the CSS-DETECT entry: SEED 7 was the marginal one there and is
#   the passing one here. Seeds are tied to the EXACT synth/map netlist — a seed that
#   passed (or failed) on a previous netlist carries NO information about this one. Always
#   re-sweep after a change that moves ALMs; never assume a seed's verdict transfers.
#
